{"content":[{"c":["SELA-HAMMAHLEKOTH*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Cliff in the wilderness of Maon, meaning “the Rock of Escape.” Saul, in his desire to kill David, attempted to catch him in the steep-ravined mountains of Judah, where David had fled. Saul’s attentions were diverted by a Philistine raid, thus enabling David to escape (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.23.28","r":"1Sam.23.28","rawR":"1Sam.23.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.23.28","value":"1Sam.23.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 23:28"},", ",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," mg). The wadi el-Malaqi, about eight miles (12.9 kilometers) northeast of Maon, is a suggested location for this cliff."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"SelaHammahlekoth","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 23:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.23.28","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.23.28","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.23.28"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6366baeccb4f57cf56e1a10a46b92dd1d98fadd3ff3570367097f01fb46d3dab","sourceItemName":"SelaHammahlekoth","sourceItemOrder":139,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"SelaHammahlekoth","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Sela-Hammahlekoth*","title":"Sela-Hammahlekoth*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}